Question 2. Explain your Kubernetes cluster upgrade project from planning to validation.
INTERVIEW-READY ANSWER
I first confirm the source and target versions, supported upgrade path, deprecated APIs, add-on compatibility,
maintenance window and rollback or recovery plan. I check cluster health, node readiness, workload replicas,
PodDisruptionBudgets, capacity and backups. I then follow the platform's control-plane upgrade procedure and rotate
worker nodes in batches, cordoning and draining nodes safely. After each batch I validate node readiness, system Pods,
application health, ingress, storage and monitoring. I stop if health checks fail. I would state the actual versions and
platform used in my project rather than guessing.
Question 3. Explain your HashiCorp Vault Enterprise migration and its risks.
INTERVIEW-READY ANSWER
The objective was to move from the open-source Vault deployment to Enterprise while preserving secure access to secrets
and minimizing disruption. I would describe the real source and target versions, storage backend, seal or auto-unseal
setup, authentication methods, policies, integrations and replication only if they were part of the implementation. Key
risks include data integrity, token and policy compatibility, authentication failures, seal configuration, network access and
application downtime. I would validate in a controlled environment, verify backups, plan a maintenance window, migrate
using the supported procedure, test representative clients and policies, monitor audit logs and retain a recovery plan.
Question 4. How would you safely decommission a legacy HA Vault deployment?
INTERVIEW-READY ANSWER
I would discover dependencies before shutting anything down: application clients, DNS records, load balancer targets,
authentication methods, policies, scheduled jobs, monitoring checks and automation still pointing to the old endpoint. I
would confirm workloads have moved, test access against the replacement, obtain owner sign-off, remove traffic in stages
and monitor failed requests. I would preserve required backups and audit records, then decommission through change
control. Evidence includes dependency checks, application tests, monitoring and confirmation that no clients still use the
legacy endpoint.
Question 5. Your resume mentions 70% lower image retrieval latency and 30% lower
deployment-related operational expenses. Explain the result.
INTERVIEW-READY ANSWER
The work involved optimizing JFrog Artifactory storage and retrieval using AWS S3-backed cache storage. I would explain
