5. Jenkins and CI/CD
Question 25. A Jenkins Maven build that worked yesterday now fails. How do you
troubleshoot?
INTERVIEW-READY ANSWER
I inspect console output and find the first meaningful error. I check the triggering commit, Jenkins agent, Java and Maven
versions, `pom.xml`, dependency repository access, credentials and disk space. I compare with the last successful build
and reproduce on a clean agent. I classify it as code, agent, dependency, network or repository failure and fix the cause
rather than repeatedly rerunning.
Question 26. Design a Jenkins pipeline from Git commit to production.
INTERVIEW-READY ANSWER
I would use stages for checkout, compile, unit tests, static analysis and quality gate, package, publish artifact, Docker
build, image scan, registry push, deploy to test, smoke tests, approval and production deploy. I use controlled agents,
credentials store or secrets manager, immutable artifact tags, archived reports, timeouts and notifications. I promote the
same tested artifact across environments.
Question 27. Write a simple Declarative Jenkinsfile for Maven.
INTERVIEW-READY ANSWER
This is a minimal example; the real agent, tool names and credential IDs must match the team's Jenkins configuration.
pipeline {
  agent any
  tools {
    maven 'Maven-3'
    jdk 'JDK-17'
  }
  stages {
    stage('Checkout') {
      steps { checkout scm }
    }
