Question 39. Explain a multi-stage Docker build for Java.
INTERVIEW-READY ANSWER
The build stage uses Maven and a JDK to compile and package the application. The runtime stage uses a smaller JRE
image and copies only the JAR. This excludes Maven, compiler tools and source from the final image. I pin base versions
and run as non-root.
FROM maven:3.9-eclipse-temurin-17 AS build
WORKDIR /app
COPY pom.xml .
COPY src ./src
RUN mvn -B clean package -DskipTests
FROM eclipse-temurin:17-jre
WORKDIR /app
RUN useradd --system --uid 10001 appuser
COPY --from=build /app/target/*.jar app.jar
USER 10001
EXPOSE 8080
ENTRYPOINT ["java", "-jar", "app.jar"]
