Question 41. It works on your laptop but fails on the server. What differs?
INTERVIEW-READY ANSWER
I compare image digest, CPU architecture, environment variables, mounts, permissions, DNS/network, secrets, resource
limits, runtime and external dependencies. I deploy the same immutable image digest that passed testing rather than an
untracked local build.
Question 42. How do you run containers securely?
INTERVIEW-READY ANSWER
I use minimal trusted images, non-root users, no privileged mode, dropped capabilities, read-only filesystems where
possible, restricted mounts and network, resource limits, patched dependencies, image scans and secrets from a runtime
secret store.
8. Kubernetes and Helm
Question 43. A production Pod is in CrashLoopBackOff. Walk through your investigation.
INTERVIEW-READY ANSWER
I run `kubectl describe pod` to inspect events, restart count, probes and termination reason. I check current and previous
logs, then inspect image, command, environment, ConfigMaps, Secrets, volumes, resource limits and dependencies. If
OOMKilled, I review memory usage and limits; if a probe fails, I verify path, port and startup timing. I fix the root cause and
verify healthy replicas.
